{
  "_notes": "Brazilian Portuguese taxonomy. 10 grammar + 10 vocabulary subs, effort-balanced and mirroring the FR structure so the runtime needs no per-language code paths. Key BR-PT-specific choices: (1) replaced FR's 'relative_pronouns' sub with 'ser_vs_estar' — the single biggest BR-PT learner struggle and not a parallel of any FR sub. (2) Subjunctive sub explicitly includes 'futuro do subjuntivo' patterns, unique to PT and used heavily after se/quando/enquanto with future reference. (3) Past tenses center on pretérito perfeito vs imperfeito — the FR passé-composé vs imparfait analog but with distinct triggers. (4) Complex sentences folds gerund-vs-infinitive (BR 'estou falando', EU 'estou a falar') since it crosses sub boundaries. (5) Vocabulary patterns localized: CPF/RG/CLT/SUS/Receita Federal replace FR's CAF/impôts. (6) 'tu' is absent from the pronoun patterns — BR informal uses você/vocês universally, and a regional 'tu' without agreement would confuse learners.",
  "_language": "pt-BR",

